THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

The MIT grant above covers the source in this repository. It does not, and
cannot, relicense anything this project merely depends on. Three notes for
anyone forking, deploying, or running this for a city:

1. Runtime dependencies are permissively licensed (MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD /
   ISC) and retain their own terms and copyright notices. Notable ones that
   ship in the built client: MapLibre GL (BSD-3-Clause), deck.gl (MIT), Cesium
   (Apache-2.0), AG Grid Community (MIT), GSAP (standard "no charge" licence).
   `pnpm-lock.yaml` is the authoritative list of what is actually installed.

2. No AGPL-licensed code is a dependency of the application or of the detector
   service, and that is deliberate rather than incidental. AGPL-3.0's
   network-use clause reaches a hosted product, so `services/detector/`
   excludes Ultralytics YOLOv8/v11 and any checkpoint derived from them by
   policy; the reasoning is in `services/detector/README.md` and the licence
   gate is stated at the top of `services/detector/requirements.txt`.

   The two exceptions are demo-only capture scripts —
   `services/detector/export_detections.py` and `render_demo.py` — which import
   `ultralytics` (AGPL-3.0). Neither is imported by the service, neither is
   installed by `requirements.txt`, and neither runs in any deployment. They
   exist to regenerate a committed artifact. If you choose to run them, you are
   running AGPL software locally and its terms apply to what you do with it.

3. Detector model weights are NOT vendored here and are not covered by this
   licence. A checkpoint carries its own terms, which are frequently more
   restrictive than the architecture's. Verify the licence of whatever
   checkpoint you select at the moment you select it — do not treat any model
   named in this repository's documentation as settled — and record the choice
   and its licence in an ADR under `docs/decisions/`.
